equirement explicitly says not to introduce it into comments. So after my change, only the call site line matches. Good.\n\nLet me also verify requirement 4b: `grep -n 'NewReassignExecutionStep' -A 4 pkg/factory/factory.go | grep -c 'assigneeSentryAnalyzerAgent'` must print exactly `1`. After my fix, the window contains `assigneeSentryAnalyzerAgent` once (line N+2). Good.\n\nNow, there's an important subtlety about the call-site format and `golines --max-len=100`. The requirement says \"Keep the call multi-line exactly as shown — one argument per line.\" After `golines`, will the multi-line format be preserved? The line `steps.NewExecutionStep(runner, prompts.BuildExecutionInstructions(), envContext),` — let me count its length. Actually golines merges short lines; but the requirement 9 says after `make precommit`, re-run the mechanical checks to confirm the reformatting did not collapse the multi-line call site. So golines might collapse it if it fits on one line. Let me think:\n\nThe whole call:\n```go\n\texecution := steps.NewReassignExecutionStep(\n\t\tsteps.NewExecutionStep(runner, prompts.BuildExecutionInstructions(), envContext),\n\t\tassigneeSentryAnalyzerAgent,\n\t\tstring(taskTypeSentryDeepAnalyzer),\n\t)\n```\n\nIf golines were to merge, it would produce:\n```go\n\texecution := steps.NewReassignExecutionStep(steps.NewExecutionStep(runner, prompts.BuildExecutionInstructions(), envContext), assigneeSentryAnalyzerAgent, string(taskTypeSentryDeepAnalyzer))\n```\n\nThat's way over 100 chars, so golines won't merge it. The requirement says verification 3/4b must still pass after precommit. Since the merged form would exceed 100 chars, golines keeps the multi-line form. \n\nBut actually — golines might reformat the arguments differently (e.g., if the first arg line is under 100 chars, it stays; gofmt won't touch multi-line call args). Let me count the first arg line: `\\t\\tsteps.NewExecutionStep(runner, prompts.BuildExecutionInstructions(), envContext),` = 2 ta